1️⃣ Node Up / Down Status
up{job="node-exporter"} == 0
______________________________

Explanation:

up metric → 1 if the target is reachable, 0 if down

Filters node-exporter job

Shows nodes that are down

For running nodes:
_________________________-
up{job="node-exporter"} == 1
_________________________________________-----------------------
2️⃣ Node CPU Usage (%)
100 - (avg by (instance) (rate(node_cpu_seconds_total{mode="idle"}[5m])) * 100)
_______________________________________

Explanation:

CPU idle → subtract from 100 to get CPU used

Aggregated by instance (node)

3️⃣ Node Memory Usage (%)
100 * (1 - (node_memory_MemAvailable_bytes / node_memory_MemTotal_bytes))

______________________________________________________
Explanation:

Shows memory usage as a percentage

MemAvailable accounts for buffers and cache

4️⃣ Node Disk Usage (%)
100 * (node_filesystem_size_bytes{mountpoint="/"} - node_filesystem_avail_bytes{mountpoint="/"}) / node_filesystem_size_bytes{mountpoint="/"}

______________________________________________
Explanation:

Checks root / filesystem usage

Can adjust mountpoint for other disks

5️⃣ Node Network Traffic

Received bytes per second:

rate(node_network_receive_bytes_total{device!="lo"}[5m])

_________________________________-
Transmitted bytes per second:

rate(node_network_transmit_bytes_total{device!="lo"}[5m])


Explanation:

Excludes loopback interface

Helps detect network spikes

6️⃣ Node Disk I/O
rate(node_disk_reads_completed_total[5m])
rate(node_disk_writes_completed_total[5m])

_____________________________________-
Shows read/write operations per second

7️⃣ Node Ready Condition (Kubernetes)
count(kube_node_status_condition{condition="Ready", status="true"} == 1)

+++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
Explanation:

True → node is ready

False → node is NotReady

For alerting:

kube_node_status_condition{condition="Ready", status="true"} == 0

______________________________________________________________-------------
Fires alert if a node is down

8️⃣ Node CPU Saturation / Load Average
node_load1 / count(node_cpu_seconds_total{mode="system"}) by (instance)


Normalizes load with CPU cores

Useful to see if node is overloaded

✅ Interview Tips

up metric → simplest way to see node health

kube_node_status_condition → for Kubernetes-aware monitoring

Aggregate by instance or node label

Combine CPU/Memory/Disk → node capacity dashboard
